aether-dtsuhd
=============

Pure Rust DTS-UHD (DTS:X Profile 2) parser and decoder.

Sources used (all public, downloaded to /tmp/aether-dtsuhd-ref during development):

  * ETSI TS 103 491 V1.2.1 (2019-05), "DTS-UHD Audio Format; Delivery of Channels,
    Objects and Ambisonic Sound Fields", https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/103400_103499/103491/01.02.01_60/ts_103491v010201p.pdf
    This is the only normative source. V1.1.1 (2017-04) was read as well to look for the
    missing compute_unmasked_levels() definition (it is absent there too).
    ETSI publishes no accompanying zip with tables or reference code for this specification
    (the deliver directory holds the two PDFs only).
  * ETSI TS 102 114 V1.6.1 (2019-08), "DTS Coherent Acoustics; Core and Extensions with
    Additional Profiles", clause 8.5.4: the 128 entry LAR to reflection coefficient table
    (src/lfe.rs RC_TABLE_Q16), used because TS 103 491 refers to PREDICTOR_QUANTIZATION_COEFF
    without defining it.
  * The bitstream of the lab sample "DTS-UHD DTSX P2 Sample.mp4" (sample entry dtsx) was
    inspected to resolve places where the specification text is wrong or silent; each case is
    listed in DESIGN.md together with the measurement that supports it.

Not used: any code from FFmpeg, libdts, DTS/Xperi SDKs or leaked material. FFmpeg's DTS-UHD
demuxer/parser was not consulted. The tables in src/tables_gen.rs are transcribed mechanically
from the PDF text by tools/gen_tables.py (ETSI copyright applies to the specification text; the
numeric constants are reproduced because they are required for interoperability).

